+# Design analysis for the D11/0 + D14/0 combo
+# -------------------------------------------
+# concretization_and_trace:
+# - The canvas is still a 29x29 grid made from a 7x7 lattice of 3x3 cell interiors
+#   separated by 1-pixel divider lines. Most cells show one majority template. A
+#   small visible subset shows one minority template.
+# - Concrete example: let the minority interior be
+#     [[m, m, m],
+#      [m, s, m],
+#      [m, s, m]]
+#   where `m` is the minority-only color and `s` is the shared color. The active
+#   mask is therefore
+#     [[1, 1, 1],
+#      [1, 0, 1],
+#      [1, 0, 1]].
+# - Original task: choose an in-bounds offset such as `(top, left) = (2, 3)` and
+#   stamp whole-cell copies of the minority template at the active positions. The
+#   3x3 enlarged block stays inside rows/cols 0..6.
+# - D11 alone changes the stamped template to
+#     [[a, a, a],
+#      [a, s, a],
