+# - D14 alone changes placement to toroidal addressing. With `(top, left) = (6, 5)`,
+#   local cell `(0, 0)` lands at global `(6, 5)`, `(1, 0)` wraps to `(0, 5)`, and
+#   `(2, 2)` wraps to `(1, 0)`.
+# - The combo must do both at once: locate the enlarged 3x3 stencil on the torus,
+#   then write the recolored template at wrapped active positions and the majority
+#   template at wrapped inactive positions. The visible difference from the original
+#   is therefore dual: border crossing and palette translation happen in the same
+#   enlarged object.
+#
